WEBVTT

00:00:09.883 --> 00:00:16.815
On 17 June 1775, British troops attacked American positions on the Charlestown peninsula,

00:00:16.815 --> 00:00:18.106
north of Boston.

00:00:18.219 --> 00:00:20.933
The fighting was mostly on Breed’s Hill,

00:00:20.933 --> 00:00:24.594
though it is remembered as the Battle of Bunker Hill.

00:00:24.707 --> 00:00:30.676
The British won the ground, but about 1,050 of their men were killed or wounded.

00:00:30.789 --> 00:00:33.500
American losses were about 450.

00:00:33.613 --> 00:00:36.160
The British set fire to Charlestown.
